0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-shape-of-the-problem","title":"The shape of the problem"},{"depth":2,"url":"#why-workers-can-be-treated-as-disposable","title":"Why workers can be treated as disposable"},{"depth":2,"url":"#draining-for-the-shutdown-you-know-about","title":"Draining, for the shutdown you know about"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-the-scheduler-remembers-and-what-it-forgets","title":"What the scheduler remembers, and what it forgets"},{"depth":2,"url":"#the-signal-you-scale-on","title":"The signal you scale on"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-the-repository-ships-and-what-it-doesnt","title":"What the repository ships, and what it doesn't"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-no-human-in-the-loop-actually-means","title":"What \"no human in the loop\" actually means"},{"depth":2,"url":"#common-questions","title":"Common questions"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Autonomous operation"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"What it takes for a build farm to grow and shrink with demand without anyone watching it: which properties Forge gives you, which pieces you assemble yourself, and where the seams are."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," whoever would otherwise be paged about the build farm.\n",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}]," an accurate picture of how close Forge\ngets you to a hands-off farm, and exactly which parts you build. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}],"\nabout fifteen minutes."]}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-shape-of-the-problem","children":"The shape of the problem"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Build load is spiky in a way that punishes static capacity. It is near zero at\nnight, ragged through the morning, and vicious in the hour before a release. A\nfarm sized for the peak is idle most of the time and expensive all of the time.\nA farm sized for the average has a queue during every moment anybody cares\nabout."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"The way out is a farm that changes size on its own. That is not a Forge\nfeature you switch on. It's a property that emerges when the components have\nthe right characteristics, and most of this page is about which characteristics\nthose are and which ones you have to supply."}],"\n",["$","$L6",null,{"as":"h2","id":"why-workers-can-be-treated-as-disposable","children":"Why workers can be treated as disposable"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Autoscaling only works if adding and removing a machine is uneventful. Three\nproperties of the worker make it so."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Workers hold no authoritative state."}]," A worker executes actions and writes\nresults to the CAS. Everything durable lives in the store, not on the worker, so\na worker that vanishes takes nothing with it that isn't reproducible."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Workers announce themselves."}]," A worker dials the scheduler and registers,\nrather than the scheduler being told a list of workers. Starting five more is\nenough; there is no membership to update. That's why\n",["$","$L7",null,{"href":"/how-to/run-multiple-workers","children":"running multiple workers"}]," is mostly a matter of\nstarting more processes."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Lost work is retried, not lost."}]," When a worker disappears mid-action, the\nscheduler notices, increments an attempt counter, and requeues the action,\nwith its worker affinity cleared, so it goes to whichever worker is free rather\nthan waiting for a machine that is gone."]}],"\n",["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-scheduler/src/simple_scheduler_state_manager.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-scheduler/src/simple_scheduler_state_manager.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-scheduler/src/simple_scheduler_state_manager.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":["$L8","update_operation"]}],"\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e","\n","$L1f","\n","$L20","\n","$L21","\n","$L22","\n","$L23","\n","$L24","\n","$L25","\n","$L26","\n","$L27","\n","$L28","\n","$L29","\n","$L2a","\n","$L2b","\n","$L2c","\n","$L2d","\n","$L2e"]}],"$L2f"]}],["$L30","$L31"],"$L32"]}],"isPartial":"$@33","staleTime":"$34","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L35","isPartial":"$@36","staleTime":"$34","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L37","isPartial":"$@38","staleTime":"$34","varyParams":"$39"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@3a","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@3b"}
